text:
{
"opening": "The boltons library is releasing version 19.1.0, which introduces several enhancements to its utility modules. The glom consumer project must update its dependency on boltons to leverage these new capabilities and ensure compatibility with the updated public API.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m08",
"text": "In the boltons library, the OneToOne class must support initialization with non-unique one-to-one inputs without raising errors, ensuring that FastIterOrderedMultiDict and unique functions handle such cases correctly."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "In the boltons library, the FunctionBuilder class's get_defaults_dict method must include keyword-only argument defaults in its output, and the formatargandannotation function must be available as part of the vendored inspect_formatargspec implementation."
},
{
"id": "m12c",
"text": "When observed through glom's tests, the boltons library's FunctionBuilder class must expose a get_arg_names method and ensure its get_defaults_dict method includes kwonly argument defaults, while formatargandannotation remains accessible via the vendored inspect_formatargspec."
},
{
"id": "m19",
"text": "In the boltons library, the difference_update method must support right subtraction operations by implementing __rsub__, allowing it to work correctly when called from the right side of an operation."
},
{
"id": "m22",
"text": "In the glom project, the core specification types Auto, Check, Fill, First, Inspect, Iter, Let, Spec, and TType must remain functional, and utility functions like all, chunked, dropwhile, fill, filter, first, flatten, glom, and glomit must continue to process data structures as expected under the updated boltons dependency."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure that the boltons release incorporates these changes and that glom is tested against this new version to verify seamless integration."
}
